# Design system

The Figma source of truth is **❖ SberUm UI**.

Source file:
https://www.figma.com/design/3sLyD0uikSYhlQMoyMCRdV/✦-SberUm-UI

fileKey: `3sLyD0uikSYhlQMoyMCRdV`

libraryKey:
`lk-b9c844e51f28ab5af108f9e787e2e2be0af12babcadc2e29824c3edb52e219075512780fb225f8186cba479333c81940303017778bbbf273b63f4291320c7149`

Always pull tokens and components from this file via MCP (`search_design_system` scoped with `includeLibraryKeys`, `get_variable_defs`, `get_design_context`). Do not invent tokens. Do not use any other UI kit.

Before implementing UI:

1. identify the UI Kit components used in the referenced Figma design;
2. identify their variants and properties;
3. identify relevant design tokens / Figma variables;
4. map the Figma components to the closest existing code equivalents.

# Component reuse

Always use an existing UI Kit component when an equivalent component exists.

Do NOT recreate existing UI Kit components with:
- raw HTML;
- custom CSS;
- Tailwind utility combinations;
- local components.

# Tokens

Never invent:

- colors;
- spacing;
- typography;
- border radii;
- shadows;
- breakpoints.

Use existing design tokens.

Do not use hardcoded visual values when an equivalent design token exists.

# Missing components

If the Figma design contains something that does not exist in the kit:

1. identify the missing component;
2. identify the closest existing SberUm UI component;
3. use the closest component if the difference is insignificant for the prototype;
4. otherwise create a one-off in the prototype `components/` folder.

Never add one-offs to a shared kit.

# Variants

Respect Figma component properties.

For example:

Figma:
Button
- type: primary
- size: medium
- state: default

Code:
`<Button variant="primary" size="medium">`
